From 7843d2274935a4d326f6377a110ef4c82de85ef0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:40:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(490): 3D boxes in the Jaquette view, multilingual
 back reader, opening on Play
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Box card style of the games carousel shows each game as a box of its
console's family (DVD/Blu-ray keep case, PlayStation jewel case, UMD,
DS/3DS/Switch/Vita cases, Mega Drive clamshell, cardboard cartridge boxes),
built with Matrix4 faces like the library's 3D book covers. Tapping the
centred box (or Up) opens a full-screen viewer: free 360° turn, tilt,
pinch zoom with pan, Front/Back/Reset, a stable low-perspective reading
pose. Play opens the box (disc in its hub, cartridge or card lifted out)
then hands the game to the library's usual launch with all its checks;
a single launch, Reduce Motion fade, opening can be turned off, a stuck
or failed rendering never blocks the game.

Box faces (back, spine, disc/cartridge scan) are fetched from ScreenScraper
through the scraper's own client, validation and quota, with a
credential-free per-game manifest of every edition (region, presumed
language, MD5/SHA-1), downloaded once and readable offline. The back can
be read in NeoStation's twelve languages: a scan published for the
reading language when one exists, else on-device Vision recognition and
Apple Translation (new neo_box_reader plugin), cached per scan.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
